{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Population Variation Analysis\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo generates a population of agents using the model's initialization routines and analyses the statistical properties of key attributes — resilience, affect, resources, and PSS-10. It computes descriptive statistics (mean, SD, skewness, kurtosis, CV, IQR), checks bounds enforcement, measures population diversity, validates reproducibility across runs, and tests edge case robustness.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "54f406bc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.agent import Person"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Helper: Mock Model"
      ],
      "id": "64ee6cb1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: mock\n",
        "class MockModel:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, seed=None):\n",
        "        self.seed = seed\n",
        "        self.agents = []\n",
        "        self.register_agent = lambda x: None\n",
        "        self.rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)"
      ],
      "id": "mock",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Generate Population"
      ],
      "id": "113083b2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: generate\n",
        "demo_config = {\n",
        "    \"initial_resilience_mean\": 0.6, \"initial_resilience_sd\": 0.15,\n",
        "    \"initial_affect_mean\": 0.1, \"initial_affect_sd\": 0.25,\n",
        "    \"initial_resources_mean\": 0.7, \"initial_resources_sd\": 0.12,\n",
        "    \"stress_probability\": 0.5, \"coping_success_rate\": 0.5, \"subevents_per_day\": 3,\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "agents = []\n",
        "for i in range(500):\n",
        "    model = MockModel(seed=1000 + i)\n",
        "    agent = Person(model, demo_config)\n",
        "    agents.append(agent)\n",
        "\n",
        "resilience = np.array([a.resilience for a in agents])\n",
        "affect = np.array([a.affect for a in agents])\n",
        "resources = np.array([a.resources for a in agents])\n",
        "pss10 = np.array([a.pss10 for a in agents])"
      ],
      "id": "generate",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Population Statistics"
      ],
      "id": "51830525"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: stats\n",
        "def describe(values, name):\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{name}:\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Mean: {np.mean(values):.3f}  SD: {np.std(values, ddof=1):.3f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Range: [{np.min(values):.3f}, {np.max(values):.3f}]\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Median: {np.median(values):.3f}  IQR: {np.percentile(values, 75) - np.percentile(values, 25):.3f}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"  Skewness: {pd.Series(values).skew():.3f}  Kurtosis: {pd.Series(values).kurtosis():.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "describe(resilience, \"Resilience\")\n",
        "describe(affect, \"Affect\")\n",
        "describe(resources, \"Resources\")\n",
        "describe(pss10, \"PSS-10\")"
      ],
      "id": "stats",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Bounds Checks"
      ],
      "id": "21c2d75f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: bounds\n",
        "all_in_bounds = all(0 <= a.resilience <= 1 and -1 <= a.affect <= 1 and 0 <= a.resources <= 1 for a in agents)\n",
        "print(f\"All agents within valid bounds: {all_in_bounds}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "unique_res = len(set(np.round(resilience, 3)))\n",
        "unique_aff = len(set(np.round(affect, 3)))\n",
        "print(f\"Unique resilience values: {unique_res}  Unique affect values: {unique_aff}\")"
      ],
      "id": "bounds",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Population variation analysis ensures that the agent initialization produces realistic diversity. If all agents were nearly identical, the simulation would lack emergent complexity. The skewness and kurtosis diagnostics reveal whether attribute distributions match real-world patterns, and bounds enforcement guarantees numerical stability throughout the simulation lifecycle."
      ],
      "id": "a6396cb1"
    }
  ],
